{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340792",
      "title": "Validating User Input With Help Of The useFormState Hook",
      "lectureOrder": 172,
      "videoOrder": 159,
      "sourceHash": "7de2bdc38f9ea668f2aada9c169defa3e7f9a53c0c0d404b2cd0bbfbb97c6997",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 2.97,
          "en": "So now that we improved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "this form submission experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 7.56,
          "en": "I wanna improve it even further.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.56,
          "end": 12.24,
          "en": "And I wanna make sure that we actually also tell the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 16.02,
          "en": "if invalid data has been entered because at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.02,
          "end": 18.87,
          "en": "I would be able to submit an empty form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 21.903,
          "en": "and that's, of course, not how it should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.22,
          "end": 25.8,
          "en": "Now, one way of adding validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.8,
          "end": 29.37,
          "en": "is that we simply add some extra attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.37,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "to our form elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 34.08,
          "en": "The required attribute, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.08,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "can be added to all the inputs and text areas",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 41.76,
          "en": "to make sure that the browser shows an error automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "without us doing anything if such a field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 47.763,
          "en": "that's marked as required is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 50.55,
          "en": "That's useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.55,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "and something you definitely should consider doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 57.78,
          "en": "because it's a quick and easy way of making your form safer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.78,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "and giving the user some feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 64.88,
          "en": "But it's not enough because this can always be disabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 68.07,
          "en": "So here if I add it, a user would be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.07,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "to inspect that form element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.14,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "and simply remove that required prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 77.043,
          "en": "that required attribute, in the browser developer tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "Of course, not all users know about these tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "but a lot of users do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "And therefore with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 87.36,
          "en": "I now would be able to submit the invalid form again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 89.1,
          "en": "So that's not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 90.53999999999999,
          "en": "It's a good first step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.53999999999999,
          "end": 93.45,
          "en": "to improve the user experience, but not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.45,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "Therefore, you should actually also always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "validate submitted data on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 100.44,
          "en": "because that's the only place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 104.763,
          "en": "where the user can't do anything about your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.78,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "Hence, you should also validate the submitted data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 112.02000000000001,
          "en": "in that server action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "So here I wanna add a if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 117.24000000000001,
          "en": "and check if title is maybe undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.24000000000001,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "or if title has a length,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "maybe after trimming it to remove excess white space,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 128.073,
          "en": "of zero, which means it would be an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129,
          "end": 131.22,
          "en": "In that case, I have an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.22,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "The same is true if the content does not exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.88,
          "end": 136.143,
          "en": "or is an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 139.82999999999998,
          "en": "And if I don't have an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.82999999999998,
          "end": 142.56,
          "en": "so if that's undefined or something like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.56,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "I also wanna return an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "So when one of these three if checks is met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.86,
          "end": 150.633,
          "en": "I wanna return an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.68,
          "end": 153.75,
          "en": "Or actually, what I wanna do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.75,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "is I wanna create an errors array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "and then I wanna add new error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "for every check that fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "So here for the first check, I wanna add a new message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "to that array of error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 172.947,
          "en": "that, for example, says, \"Title is required.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.12,
          "end": 176.88,
          "en": "And then for the second check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.88,
          "end": 180.24,
          "en": "I wanna add a message that says, \"Content is required.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.24,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "And for the third check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 185.19,
          "en": "I add a message that says, \"Image is required.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 186.39,
          "en": "That would be one way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.39,
          "end": 189.783,
          "en": "of constructing such an error message array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 194.7,
          "en": "But of course, having that array here is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.7,
          "end": 196.62,
          "en": "We also need to get it back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.62,
          "end": 199.11,
          "en": "to the client side to update the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 202.17000000000002,
          "en": "and show those error messages to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.17000000000002,
          "end": 206.79,
          "en": "in case they did try to submit an empty or invalid form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.79,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "And how do we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "Well, it would definitely be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 216.36,
          "en": "if we could simply check here in our server action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "if this errors array has a length that's greater than zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 222.54,
          "en": "which means it's not empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.54,
          "end": 225.03300000000002,
          "en": "which means we have at least one error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.11,
          "end": 229.86,
          "en": "And if in that case, we could simply return an object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.86,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "from our server action that includes that errors array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 235.233,
          "en": "as a property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "That would be nice to do, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 240.48,
          "en": "If we could just return such an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.48,
          "end": 242.88,
          "en": "and then we could handle it on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 242.88,
          "end": 246.63,
          "en": "And it turns out we can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 250.08,
          "en": "NextJS and React got us covered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 254.64,
          "en": "because React offers another form-related hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.64,
          "end": 257.34,
          "en": "the useFormState hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.34,
          "end": 260.52,
          "en": "So not useFormStatus, which we used before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.52,
          "end": 261.37,
          "en": "but useFormState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 264.93,
          "en": "And that's a hook that you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.93,
          "end": 269.25,
          "en": "to update the form-related UI you're showing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.25,
          "end": 271.8,
          "en": "to the user based on some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "that may be changed upon the submission of a form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "which is a complex way of saying you can use this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 283.14,
          "en": "to output any data you return from your formAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.14,
          "end": 285.753,
          "en": "from your server action in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.86,
          "end": 290.97,
          "en": "Therefore, here, I'll import this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.97,
          "end": 295.97,
          "en": "useFormState hook from react-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 298.14,
          "end": 303.14,
          "en": "Again, it's imported from react-dom, not from React itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 307.29,
          "en": "And we can now call this hook in our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.29,
          "end": 311.313,
          "en": "that outputs the form, useFormState like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.9,
          "end": 316.32,
          "en": "So now I'm not calling it in some nested component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.32,
          "end": 318.75,
          "en": "as I did it with useFormStatus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.75,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "which we called in the formSubmit component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "but instead directly in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 326.793,
          "en": "that also outputs the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.81,
          "end": 332.81,
          "en": "Now, useFormState then takes a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.85,
          "end": 335.67,
          "en": "or actually, two values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.67,
          "end": 340.42,
          "en": "And the first value this hook accepts is the formAction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 341.28,
          "end": 344.4,
          "en": "that should actually eventually be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 345.993,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.01,
          "end": 348.69,
          "en": "So therefore, I'll actually call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.69,
          "end": 350.95,
          "en": "after defining that formAction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.23,
          "end": 356.07,
          "en": "and then I will pass that formAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 356.07,
          "end": 359.55,
          "en": "this createPost function to useFormState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 359.55,
          "end": 361.65,
          "en": "as a first argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 361.65,
          "end": 363.3,
          "en": "I'm not executing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 363.3,
          "end": 366.81,
          "en": "Instead I'm just passing a pointer to this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.81,
          "end": 368.973,
          "en": "as a first argument to useFormState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 370.53,
          "end": 373.17,
          "en": "And then as a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.17,
          "end": 376.26,
          "en": "we pass some initial form state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.26,
          "end": 380.97,
          "en": "that should be used if the formAction has not executed yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.97,
          "end": 383.58,
          "en": "And here in my case, that will be an empty object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.58,
          "end": 387.78,
          "en": "because the form state I might eventually get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 387.78,
          "end": 391.62,
          "en": "will be this object that has an errors property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 391.62,
          "end": 395.13,
          "en": "which contains an array of error messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 395.13,
          "end": 397.84000000000003,
          "en": "That's the form state we may eventually get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 398.76,
          "end": 401.46,
          "en": "because if the form submission succeeds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 401.46,
          "end": 406.14,
          "en": "if we have valid data, we don't return any new state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 406.14,
          "end": 407.61,
          "en": "that should be shown on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 407.61,
          "end": 410.04,
          "en": "Instead, we navigate away here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 410.04,
          "end": 413.79,
          "en": "So the only other state we can achieve is this errors state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 413.79,
          "end": 417.69,
          "en": "But initially, we, of course, don't have any errors yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 417.69,
          "end": 419.94,
          "en": "because the user didn't even have a chance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 419.94,
          "end": 421.2,
          "en": "of entering something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 421.2,
          "end": 423.78,
          "en": "And therefore, my initial state for this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 423.78,
          "end": 425.67,
          "en": "should be such an empty object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 425.67,
          "end": 428.883,
          "en": "and we'll use that state in just a second, no worries.",
